1
00:01:58,060 --> 00:02:01,420
Out, all of you.

2
00:02:03,050 --> 00:02:05,790
Bastard's been meddling where he shouldn't!

3
00:02:06,230 --> 00:02:09,440
I want you and your men

4
00:02:10,330 --> 00:02:11,400
gone.

5
00:02:12,240 --> 00:02:15,280
And you will make this right.

6
00:02:18,730 --> 00:02:19,850
Wait outside.

7
00:02:19,850 --> 00:02:21,380
- Lord Commander. - Now!

8
00:02:42,440 --> 00:02:44,380
- Lord Commander. - Leave us.

9
00:02:46,480 --> 00:02:47,760
What did you do?

10
00:02:48,770 --> 00:02:49,930
I followed him.

11
00:02:51,030 --> 00:02:53,400
He took the baby into the woods, the newborn.

12
00:02:53,400 --> 00:02:55,260
What business is that of yours?

13
00:02:55,260 --> 00:02:56,740
No, you don't understand.

14
00:02:56,740 --> 00:02:58,620
He's killing them, all the boys.

15
00:03:04,770 --> 00:03:06,040
You know.

16
00:03:09,830 --> 00:03:14,530
The wildlings serve crueler gods than you or I.

17
00:03:15,760 --> 00:03:19,350
Those boys are Craster's offerings.

18
00:03:19,350 --> 00:03:20,530
Offerings?

19
00:03:20,530 --> 00:03:23,100
He's murdering his own children. He's a monster.

20
00:03:23,100 --> 00:03:25,410
Aye, many a time that monster has been the difference

21
00:03:25,420 --> 00:03:28,030
between life and death for our rangers.

22
00:03:28,030 --> 00:03:29,890
Your uncle among them.

23
00:03:30,730 --> 00:03:33,550
We have other wars to fight out there.

24
00:03:34,310 --> 00:03:38,670
Like it or not, we need men like Craster.

25
00:03:43,720 --> 00:03:44,730
I...

26
00:03:45,170 --> 00:03:46,560
I saw it.

27
00:03:49,640 --> 00:03:50,730
I saw...

28
00:03:53,350 --> 00:03:55,320
Something take that child.

29
00:03:56,750 --> 00:03:57,750
Yeah.

30
00:03:57,750 --> 00:03:59,280
Whatever it was,

31
00:04:00,690 --> 00:04:02,980
I daresay you'll see it again.

32
00:04:04,880 --> 00:04:07,780
Now ready my horse.

33
00:04:07,780 --> 00:04:09,540
We leave at dawn.

34
00:04:15,260 --> 00:04:16,970
Don't lose it again.

35
00:04:41,560 --> 00:04:42,490
Gilly.

36
00:04:46,230 --> 00:04:47,570
You're leaving.

37
00:04:48,390 --> 00:04:52,000
I... I wanted to give you something.

38
00:04:56,010 --> 00:04:57,480
It belonged to my mother.

39
00:04:59,830 --> 00:05:02,000
- I can't take it. - Please.

40
00:05:02,790 --> 00:05:04,260
I want you to.

41
00:05:07,510 --> 00:05:09,200
My mother used it for sewing.

42
00:05:10,340 --> 00:05:13,870
She'd let me sit with her in her chamber while she sewed

43
00:05:14,520 --> 00:05:16,040
and I'd read to her.

44
00:05:18,740 --> 00:05:21,120
My father put a stop to it when he found out.

45
00:05:23,070 --> 00:05:25,040
It's the only thing I have of hers.

46
00:05:26,070 --> 00:05:28,520
She gave it to me before I left for the Wall.

47
00:05:30,200 --> 00:05:31,240
You...

48
00:05:31,690 --> 00:05:33,130
You shouldn't give it away.

49
00:05:33,130 --> 00:05:35,130
I'm not giving it away.

50
00:05:36,780 --> 00:05:38,280
I'm giving it to you.

51
00:05:40,680 --> 00:05:42,430
Keep it safe for me.

52
00:05:43,400 --> 00:05:44,900
Till I come back.

53
00:06:03,490 --> 00:06:04,430
Hodor.

54
00:06:04,950 --> 00:06:06,030
Hodor.

55
00:06:06,930 --> 00:06:10,050
Rouse Bran, will you? It's time for his lessons.

56
00:06:42,720 --> 00:06:44,410
Every night it's the same.

57
00:06:45,790 --> 00:06:47,210
I'm walking

58
00:06:47,850 --> 00:06:49,770
and running, but...

59
00:06:52,030 --> 00:06:55,170
I'm not-- I'm not me.

60
00:06:56,420 --> 00:06:58,250
I'm running through the Godswood,

61
00:06:58,260 --> 00:06:59,770
Sniffing the dirt,

62
00:07:00,410 --> 00:07:03,560
tasting blood in my mouth when I've made a fresh kill,

63
00:07:04,970 --> 00:07:06,310
Howling.

64
00:07:08,700 --> 00:07:10,650
Old nan used to tell me stories

65
00:07:10,650 --> 00:07:17,630
about magical people who could live inside stags, birds, wolves.

66
00:07:17,820 --> 00:07:20,950
That's exactly what they are, Bran... stories.

67
00:07:20,950 --> 00:07:23,480
So she was lying? They don't exist?

68
00:07:23,580 --> 00:07:25,800
Well, they may have done.

69
00:07:25,910 --> 00:07:30,420
But they're gone from the world along with much else.

70
00:07:32,430 --> 00:07:36,320
These are dreams, Bran, nothing more.

71
00:07:36,320 --> 00:07:39,050
No, my dreams are different.

72
00:07:39,050 --> 00:07:40,570
Mine are true.

73
00:07:40,720 --> 00:07:43,160
I dreamt of my father dying.

74
00:07:44,230 --> 00:07:46,100
And Rickon had the same dream.

75
00:07:46,100 --> 00:07:49,290
What about all the dreams you had that didn't come true?

76
00:07:56,820 --> 00:07:57,820
Right.

77
00:07:58,620 --> 00:08:02,120
This link is made of Valyrian steel.

78
00:08:02,880 --> 00:08:05,950
Only one maester in 100 wears it on his chain.

79
00:08:07,030 --> 00:08:10,430
It signifies that I have studied the higher mysteries.

80
00:08:10,910 --> 00:08:15,110
And all who study these mysteries try their hand at spells.

81
00:08:15,110 --> 00:08:16,740
I was no different.

82
00:08:17,200 --> 00:08:18,610
I was young.

83
00:08:19,160 --> 00:08:23,230
And what boy doesn't secretly wish for hidden powers

84
00:08:23,690 --> 00:08:26,880
to lift him out of his dull life into a special one?

85
00:08:28,090 --> 00:08:30,210
But in the end, for all my efforts,

86
00:08:30,310 --> 00:08:33,790
I got no more out of it than 1,000 boys before me.

87
00:08:35,270 --> 00:08:36,370
Come on.

88
00:08:45,050 --> 00:08:46,340
All right.

89
00:08:47,770 --> 00:08:51,790
Maybe magic once was a mighty force in the world.

90
00:08:53,860 --> 00:08:55,820
But not anymore.

91
00:08:57,430 --> 00:08:59,470
The dragons are gone.

92
00:08:59,560 --> 00:09:01,330
The giants are dead.

93
00:09:03,750 --> 00:09:06,260
And the children of the forest forgotten.

94
00:09:56,890 --> 00:09:58,800
Loras! Highgarden!

95
00:10:03,910 --> 00:10:05,020
Get him!

96
00:10:12,460 --> 00:10:15,190
Yield! I yield.

97
00:10:24,320 --> 00:10:26,560
Well fought. Approach.

98
00:10:35,940 --> 00:10:38,230
Rise. Remove your helm.

99
00:10:46,750 --> 00:10:49,410
You are all your father promised and more, my lady.

100
00:10:49,810 --> 00:10:51,830
I've seen Ser Loras bested once or twice,

101
00:10:51,830 --> 00:10:54,550
but never quite in that fashion.

102
00:10:54,660 --> 00:10:57,880
Now, now, my love. My brother fought valiantly for you.

103
00:10:59,570 --> 00:11:01,290
That he did, my Queen.

104
00:11:01,810 --> 00:11:03,850
But there can only be one champion.

105
00:11:05,200 --> 00:11:06,770
Brienne of Tarth,

106
00:11:06,770 --> 00:11:08,970
you may ask anything of me you desire.

107
00:11:08,970 --> 00:11:11,990
If it is within my power, it is yours.

108
00:11:13,740 --> 00:11:15,120
Your grace,

109
00:11:15,720 --> 00:11:19,090
I ask the honor of a place in your kingsguard.

110
00:11:19,220 --> 00:11:20,460
What?

111
00:11:20,460 --> 00:11:22,260
I will be one of your seven,

112
00:11:22,260 --> 00:11:23,600
pledge my life to yours,

113
00:11:23,600 --> 00:11:25,840
and keep you safe from all harm.

114
00:11:30,490 --> 00:11:31,620
Done.

115
00:11:32,440 --> 00:11:35,050
Rise, Brienne of the Kingsguard.

116
00:11:43,880 --> 00:11:47,110
Your grace, I have the honor to bring you lady Catelyn Stark,

117
00:11:47,110 --> 00:11:50,160
sent as an envoy by her son Robb, Lord of Winterfell.

118
00:11:50,160 --> 00:11:53,800
Lord of Winterfell and King in the North.

119
00:11:53,800 --> 00:11:56,820
Lady Catelyn. I'm pleased to see you.

120
00:11:57,420 --> 00:12:00,880
May I present my wife Margaery of House Tyrell?

121
00:12:01,970 --> 00:12:04,490
You are very welcome here, Lady Stark.

122
00:12:04,610 --> 00:12:06,670
I'm so sorry for your loss.

123
00:12:07,600 --> 00:12:09,420
You are most kind.

124
00:12:09,700 --> 00:12:11,010
My lady,

125
00:12:12,130 --> 00:12:14,480
I swear to you I will see the Lannisters answer

126
00:12:14,480 --> 00:12:16,170
for your husband's murder.

127
00:12:17,100 --> 00:12:18,940
When I take King's Landing,

128
00:12:19,760 --> 00:12:21,450
I'll bring you Joffrey's head.

129
00:12:30,120 --> 00:12:31,500
It will be enough to know

130
00:12:31,500 --> 00:12:33,580
that justice was done, my lord.

131
00:12:33,780 --> 00:12:35,260
Your grace.

132
00:12:35,830 --> 00:12:38,290
And you should kneel when you approach the king.

133
00:12:38,290 --> 00:12:41,630
There's no need for that. Lady Stark is an honored guest.

134
00:12:41,630 --> 00:12:44,120
Has your son marched against Tywin Lannister yet?

135
00:12:45,430 --> 00:12:48,150
I do not sit on my son's war councils.

136
00:12:48,150 --> 00:12:52,390
And if I did, I would not share his strategies with you.

137
00:12:52,390 --> 00:12:55,230
If Robb Stark wants a pact with us, he should come himself,

138
00:12:55,230 --> 00:12:57,180
not hide behind his mother's skirts.

139
00:12:57,190 --> 00:12:59,980
My son is fighting a war,

140
00:13:00,150 --> 00:13:02,100
not playing at one.

141
00:13:15,400 --> 00:13:16,870
Don't worry, my lady.

142
00:13:17,450 --> 00:13:19,280
Our war is just beginning.

143
00:13:33,140 --> 00:13:34,680
- Your grace. - Gerard.

144
00:13:34,680 --> 00:13:37,360
- How's your foot? - Better, your grace.

145
00:13:37,760 --> 00:13:39,750
They don't know their own size is all.

146
00:13:39,820 --> 00:13:40,840
Good man.

147
00:13:43,790 --> 00:13:45,860
I have 100,000 men at my command.

148
00:13:46,110 --> 00:13:48,310
All the might of the Stormlands and the Reach.

149
00:13:48,310 --> 00:13:51,870
And all of them young and bold like your Knight of Flowers?

150
00:13:52,910 --> 00:13:54,920
It's a game to you, isn't it?

151
00:13:55,640 --> 00:13:57,690
- I pity them. - Why?

152
00:13:57,690 --> 00:13:59,520
Because it won't last.

153
00:13:59,520 --> 00:14:03,150
Because they are the knights of summer and winter is coming.

154
00:14:05,470 --> 00:14:09,340
Brienne, escort lady Catelyn to her tent.

155
00:14:09,760 --> 00:14:12,600
- She's tired from her journey. - At once, your grace.

156
00:14:12,710 --> 00:14:15,540
- Shall I return after? - That won't be necessary.

157
00:14:15,540 --> 00:14:18,670
I would pray awhile. Alone.

158
00:14:20,050 --> 00:14:21,950
If you'll follow me, my lady.

159
00:14:24,670 --> 00:14:27,310
You fought bravely today, lady Brienne.

160
00:14:27,780 --> 00:14:29,370
I fought for my king.

161
00:14:29,980 --> 00:14:32,490
Soon I'll fight for him on the battlefield.

162
00:14:32,690 --> 00:14:34,630
Die for him if I must.

163
00:14:35,520 --> 00:14:39,300
And, if it please you, Brienne's enough.

164
00:14:40,050 --> 00:14:41,690
I'm no lady.

165
00:15:13,020 --> 00:15:14,340
What are you doing here?

166
00:15:15,080 --> 00:15:16,310
I live here.

167
00:15:17,090 --> 00:15:21,470
- Are you angry with me, brother? - You lying bitch.

168
00:15:21,470 --> 00:15:23,700
It's not my fault you didn't recognize me.

169
00:15:24,410 --> 00:15:27,220
Recognize you? How could I?

170
00:15:27,380 --> 00:15:29,050
The last time I saw you...

171
00:15:31,080 --> 00:15:33,230
You looked like a fat little boy.

172
00:15:34,150 --> 00:15:36,140
You were a fat little boy, too,

173
00:15:36,940 --> 00:15:38,840
but I recognized you.

174
00:15:39,170 --> 00:15:40,700
Why didn't you tell me?

175
00:15:40,700 --> 00:15:43,080
I wanted to see who you were first.

176
00:15:43,080 --> 00:15:44,710
And I did.

177
00:15:47,450 --> 00:15:50,010
The plans are made. It's time you heard them.

178
00:15:50,010 --> 00:15:51,620
- Father. - Father.

179
00:15:54,440 --> 00:15:56,660
The wolf pup has gone south

180
00:15:56,660 --> 00:15:59,640
with the entirety of the northern army at his back.

181
00:15:59,840 --> 00:16:02,640
While he's tangling with the lion in the westerlands,

182
00:16:02,650 --> 00:16:05,550
the north is ripe for the taking.

183
00:16:05,690 --> 00:16:09,070
The Ironborn will reave and pillage as it was in the old days

184
00:16:09,070 --> 00:16:11,040
all along the northern coast.

185
00:16:11,260 --> 00:16:14,280
We'll spread our dominion across the green lands,

186
00:16:14,280 --> 00:16:17,140
securing the Neck and everything above.

187
00:16:17,140 --> 00:16:19,830
Every stronghold will yield to us one by one.

188
00:16:19,960 --> 00:16:22,860
Winterfell may defy us for a year, but what of it?

189
00:16:22,860 --> 00:16:24,620
The rest shall be ours...

190
00:16:24,630 --> 00:16:28,200
forest, field and hall.

191
00:16:32,410 --> 00:16:35,170
Yara, my daughter, you'll take 30 longships

192
00:16:35,170 --> 00:16:37,100
to attack Deepwood Motte.

193
00:16:37,100 --> 00:16:39,140
I've always wanted a castle.

194
00:16:39,240 --> 00:16:41,080
And what's my role in all this?

195
00:16:43,280 --> 00:16:44,590
You'll take a ship to raid

196
00:16:44,590 --> 00:16:47,130
the fishing villages on the Stoney Shore.

197
00:16:47,130 --> 00:16:48,500
A ship?

198
00:16:48,910 --> 00:16:51,020
You give her 30 and I get one?

199
00:16:51,020 --> 00:16:54,510
The Sea Bitch. We thought she'd be perfect for you.

200
00:16:56,920 --> 00:16:58,270
I'm to fight fishermen?

201
00:16:58,270 --> 00:17:00,100
Be careful of their nets.

202
00:17:03,900 --> 00:17:06,340
Father, I fought with Robb Stark.

203
00:17:06,440 --> 00:17:08,010
I know his men.

204
00:17:08,160 --> 00:17:09,800
He won't give up the north so easily.

205
00:17:09,800 --> 00:17:11,400
They won't even know we're there until it's too late.

206
00:17:11,400 --> 00:17:12,710
What do you know of it, woman?

207
00:17:12,710 --> 00:17:14,310
I'm a proven warrior.

208
00:17:14,310 --> 00:17:17,820
Your brothers were warriors, both of them dead

209
00:17:17,820 --> 00:17:21,290
at the hands of those you seem so eager to protect.

210
00:17:22,930 --> 00:17:24,940
I'm not protecting anyone.

211
00:17:24,950 --> 00:17:27,120
I just wonder if it's not wiser to wait.

212
00:17:27,120 --> 00:17:30,210
Why risk going against the North if they would be our allies?

213
00:17:31,240 --> 00:17:33,580
Rise up against them and they could destroy us.

214
00:17:33,580 --> 00:17:36,190
But if we pledge fealty to them,

215
00:17:36,200 --> 00:17:38,090
they'll give us Casterly Rock.

216
00:17:38,090 --> 00:17:39,670
What are our words?

217
00:17:41,210 --> 00:17:43,240
Our words?

218
00:17:45,700 --> 00:17:48,300
- "We do not sow." - "We do not sow."

219
00:17:48,420 --> 00:17:50,130
We are ironborn.

220
00:17:50,130 --> 00:17:53,000
We're not subjects. We're not slaves.

221
00:17:53,140 --> 00:17:56,010
We do not plow the fields or toil in the mine.

222
00:17:56,010 --> 00:17:58,070
We take what is ours.

223
00:17:59,480 --> 00:18:02,690
Your time with the wolves has made you weak.

224
00:18:06,450 --> 00:18:08,930
You act as if I volunteered to go.

225
00:18:09,970 --> 00:18:12,240
You gave me away, if you remember.

226
00:18:12,320 --> 00:18:14,690
The day you bent the knee to Robert Baratheon

227
00:18:14,820 --> 00:18:16,580
after he crushed you.

228
00:18:16,580 --> 00:18:18,750
Did you take what was yours then?

229
00:18:22,870 --> 00:18:24,740
You gave me away!

230
00:18:25,570 --> 00:18:27,010
Your boy!

231
00:18:27,510 --> 00:18:29,510
Your last boy!

232
00:18:30,230 --> 00:18:33,560
You gave me away like I was some dog you didn't want anymore.

233
00:18:34,030 --> 00:18:36,950
And now you curse me because I've come home.

234
00:18:47,620 --> 00:18:50,770
You'd have our father bow down to your other family?

235
00:18:50,770 --> 00:18:53,170
I have no other family.

236
00:18:53,170 --> 00:18:54,510
Don't you?

237
00:18:56,360 --> 00:18:58,820
Make your choice, Theon, and do it quickly.

238
00:18:58,970 --> 00:19:01,500
Our ships sail with or without you.

239
00:19:13,860 --> 00:19:15,300
You won't let me leave this room.

240
00:19:15,310 --> 00:19:17,930
- You won't let me... - Shh, shh, keep your voice down.

241
00:19:21,240 --> 00:19:23,900
Why? You think your father can hear me?

242
00:19:24,590 --> 00:19:27,190
He's 300 miles away!

243
00:19:29,500 --> 00:19:32,110
I don't intend for you to stay here.

244
00:19:32,640 --> 00:19:35,630
I might be able to bring you into the castle kitchens.

245
00:19:35,960 --> 00:19:38,080
Again, only temporary.

246
00:19:39,590 --> 00:19:41,350
Every man who has tasted my cooking

247
00:19:41,350 --> 00:19:43,850
has told me what a good whore I am.

248
00:19:43,920 --> 00:19:45,830
But you wouldn't be a cook.

249
00:19:46,280 --> 00:19:48,140
You'd pose as a scullion.

250
00:19:50,030 --> 00:19:52,480
Scullion? What is a scullion?

251
00:19:53,230 --> 00:19:54,820
Kitchen wench.

252
00:19:54,970 --> 00:19:57,990
- A kitchen wench? - Yes, but...

253
00:19:57,990 --> 00:20:02,100
Cleaning pots? Is that how my lion wants to see me?

254
00:20:02,190 --> 00:20:04,830
Your lion wants to see you alive.

255
00:20:04,830 --> 00:20:07,120
We've come to a dangerous place.

256
00:20:07,120 --> 00:20:09,010
My sister wants to hurt me.

257
00:20:09,020 --> 00:20:11,160
She'll look for any weakness she can find.

258
00:20:11,170 --> 00:20:13,420
She can't know about you.

259
00:20:13,650 --> 00:20:15,330
I'm the weakness?

260
00:20:15,330 --> 00:20:17,240
It's a compliment, my lady.

261
00:20:17,370 --> 00:20:20,020
How is being a weakness a compliment?

262
00:20:23,620 --> 00:20:25,580
Language can be a bit tricky here.

263
00:20:25,580 --> 00:20:29,110
Oh, I'm too stupid to understand.

264
00:20:29,110 --> 00:20:31,220
The stupid foreign girl.

265
00:20:34,210 --> 00:20:37,350
I am not a kitchen wench.

266
00:21:02,270 --> 00:21:04,430
When will Joffrey and Sansa be married?

267
00:21:04,910 --> 00:21:07,160
Soon, darling, when the war is over.

268
00:21:07,560 --> 00:21:10,070
Mother says I'll have a new gown for the ceremony

269
00:21:10,070 --> 00:21:11,740
and another for the feast.

270
00:21:12,490 --> 00:21:15,440
But yours will be ivory since you're the bride.

271
00:21:19,990 --> 00:21:21,860
The princess just spoke to you.

272
00:21:22,170 --> 00:21:23,780
Pardon, Your grace.

273
00:21:26,580 --> 00:21:29,010
I'm sure your dress will be beautiful, Myrcella.

274
00:21:29,550 --> 00:21:32,320
I'm counting the days until the fighting is done

275
00:21:32,320 --> 00:21:35,410
and I can pledge my love to the King in sight of the gods.

276
00:21:40,220 --> 00:21:42,800
Is Joffrey going to kill Sansa's brother?

277
00:21:45,590 --> 00:21:46,900
He might.

278
00:21:49,700 --> 00:21:51,130
Would you like that?

279
00:21:53,010 --> 00:21:55,610
No. I don't think so.

280
00:21:57,240 --> 00:22:00,580
Even if he does, Sansa will do her duty.

281
00:22:02,220 --> 00:22:03,930
Won't you, little dove?

282
00:22:23,000 --> 00:22:24,270
Come in.

283
00:22:27,970 --> 00:22:29,170
Who are you?

284
00:22:29,280 --> 00:22:31,920
I'm Shae, my lady. Your new handmaiden.

285
00:22:32,910 --> 00:22:35,310
I didn't know I needed a new handmaiden.

286
00:22:37,270 --> 00:22:39,840
- You're not from here. - No.

287
00:22:46,320 --> 00:22:47,730
What are you doing?

288
00:22:47,760 --> 00:22:49,760
Waiting for you to tell me what to do.

289
00:22:49,760 --> 00:22:51,760
I shouldn't have to tell you to do things.

290
00:22:51,760 --> 00:22:53,460
You should just do them.

291
00:22:54,230 --> 00:22:55,840
What things?

292
00:22:56,570 --> 00:22:58,500
Change my linens, wash my clothing,

293
00:22:58,500 --> 00:23:01,700
scrub the floor, empty my chamber pot, brush my hair.

294
00:23:10,910 --> 00:23:12,700
- No. - You said to brush...

295
00:23:12,700 --> 00:23:14,290
Not now.

296
00:23:17,270 --> 00:23:19,140
Your chamber pot is empty.

297
00:23:20,140 --> 00:23:21,710
Clean the table.

298
00:23:27,120 --> 00:23:29,830
Have you ever been a handmaiden before?

299
00:23:30,010 --> 00:23:31,610
- Yes. - For whom?

300
00:23:31,610 --> 00:23:34,050
- Lady Zuriff. - Lady Zuriff?

301
00:23:36,090 --> 00:23:37,600
Lady zuriff.

302
00:23:38,320 --> 00:23:40,880
There is no Lady Zuriff in this city.

303
00:23:41,590 --> 00:23:43,490
She wasn't in this city.

304
00:23:43,490 --> 00:23:45,850
Well, I don't know how they did things in that city,

305
00:23:45,850 --> 00:23:48,610
but in this city, handmaidens wait on ladies,

306
00:23:48,610 --> 00:23:50,380
not the other way around.

307
00:23:50,380 --> 00:23:53,190
And I don't have time to answer 1,000 questions

308
00:23:53,190 --> 00:23:55,440
and teach you how to do your job.

309
00:23:59,020 --> 00:24:00,660
Do you want me to leave?

310
00:24:08,700 --> 00:24:10,440
Just brush my hair.

311
00:24:25,020 --> 00:24:27,500
Oh, thank the gods.

312
00:24:27,640 --> 00:24:30,320
I haven't had a proper shit in six days.

313
00:24:30,490 --> 00:24:33,140
I've encountered this problem before, my lord.

314
00:24:33,140 --> 00:24:38,390
The stresses of power often have this insalubrious effect.

315
00:24:38,390 --> 00:24:41,710
Two drops with water daily.

316
00:24:41,970 --> 00:24:43,570
Right. I'm so grateful to have a man

317
00:24:43,570 --> 00:24:46,130
of your vast knowledge and wisdom on my side.

318
00:24:46,650 --> 00:24:48,990
- Please. - Thank you, my lord.

319
00:24:54,460 --> 00:24:56,280
I can trust you, Pycelle, can I not?

320
00:24:56,280 --> 00:24:57,970
Why, yes, of course, my lord.

321
00:24:57,970 --> 00:24:59,770
These are perilous times.

322
00:25:00,160 --> 00:25:02,580
And the Crown must forge new alliances.

323
00:25:03,310 --> 00:25:07,210
And these alliances must often be sealed in matrimony.

324
00:25:07,670 --> 00:25:10,100
Matrimony, huh?

325
00:25:10,100 --> 00:25:11,410
Yes.

326
00:25:11,990 --> 00:25:14,220
I'm trusting the council with these plans,

327
00:25:14,220 --> 00:25:16,170
but the queen mustn't know.

328
00:25:16,480 --> 00:25:18,450
We can't have her meddling in affairs

329
00:25:18,460 --> 00:25:19,940
that could determine the future of the realm.

330
00:25:19,940 --> 00:25:21,350
There's too much at stake.

331
00:25:21,350 --> 00:25:23,600
Oh, yes, yes. Indeed, yes.

332
00:25:23,950 --> 00:25:27,210
I shall be silent as the grave.

333
00:25:27,720 --> 00:25:30,670
I'm brokering an alliance with House Martell of Dorne.

334
00:25:32,070 --> 00:25:35,380
Princess Myrcella will wed their youngest son when she comes of age,

335
00:25:35,480 --> 00:25:39,590
ensuring their loyalty and their army should we need it.

336
00:25:40,030 --> 00:25:43,800
Myrcella sent away to Dorne?

337
00:25:45,470 --> 00:25:48,650
But remember, the queen mustn't know.

338
00:25:49,260 --> 00:25:52,740
Ooh, "The queen mustn't know."

339
00:25:52,880 --> 00:25:56,050
I love conversations that begin this way.

340
00:25:56,550 --> 00:25:58,980
I plan to marry Princess Myrcella off

341
00:25:59,280 --> 00:26:01,010
to Theon Greyjoy.

342
00:26:02,530 --> 00:26:04,320
Theon Greyjoy?

343
00:26:05,190 --> 00:26:07,310
Forgive me, my lord, but how?

344
00:26:07,650 --> 00:26:10,410
He grew up a ward of Winterfell.

345
00:26:10,410 --> 00:26:11,800
He fights for Robb Stark.

346
00:26:11,800 --> 00:26:12,850
Precisely.

347
00:26:12,910 --> 00:26:15,610
Theon's father loathes the Starks

348
00:26:15,610 --> 00:26:18,260
and will convince the boy to come to our side.

349
00:26:19,030 --> 00:26:21,650
Greyjoy can destroy the northern army from within

350
00:26:21,650 --> 00:26:23,440
and we can have his father's ships.

351
00:26:24,500 --> 00:26:27,570
But remember, you must tell no one.

352
00:26:27,630 --> 00:26:30,720
Tell no one what?

353
00:26:31,060 --> 00:26:34,590
I plan to wed Princess Myrcella to Robin Arryn of the Vale.

354
00:26:35,920 --> 00:26:39,090
Lysa is not fond of me.

355
00:26:39,130 --> 00:26:41,450
But perhaps the promise of a royal match

356
00:26:41,450 --> 00:26:45,180
will convince her to let bygones be bygones.

357
00:26:45,180 --> 00:26:46,790
She imprisoned you.

358
00:26:47,190 --> 00:26:49,110
She tried to execute you.

359
00:26:49,110 --> 00:26:51,880
And you offer her son a princess?

360
00:26:52,300 --> 00:26:56,570
For men in our position, holding grudges can be an encumbrance,

361
00:26:56,630 --> 00:26:57,850
don't you think?

362
00:26:58,530 --> 00:27:02,140
And I suppose you want me to broker this agreement?

363
00:27:02,140 --> 00:27:03,420
Who better?

364
00:27:07,740 --> 00:27:11,950
Yes, I could sing this song to Lysa, if I cared to.

365
00:27:13,440 --> 00:27:15,120
What's in it for me?

366
00:27:16,860 --> 00:27:20,680
The gratitude of the people of Westeros for helping to end this war,

367
00:27:20,710 --> 00:27:24,460
the adoration of the king for bringing the Vale back into the fold...

368
00:27:26,730 --> 00:27:28,250
and Harrenhal.

369
00:27:28,500 --> 00:27:30,510
Harrenhal is cursed.

370
00:27:30,740 --> 00:27:32,970
Never took you for a superstitious man.

371
00:27:32,970 --> 00:27:34,880
By all means, tear it down and rebuild.

372
00:27:34,880 --> 00:27:36,540
You'll be able to afford it.

373
00:27:36,740 --> 00:27:38,970
I plan to make you lord of the riverlands.

374
00:27:41,620 --> 00:27:42,710
With a single stroke,

375
00:27:42,710 --> 00:27:44,490
you'd make me one of the greatest lords in the realm.

376
00:27:44,490 --> 00:27:47,640
You served my family well in the matter of the succession.

377
00:27:47,640 --> 00:27:50,870
So did Janos Slynt, and he was given Harrenhal, too.

378
00:27:50,870 --> 00:27:53,230
Until you snatched it away.

379
00:27:53,260 --> 00:27:55,630
I need you to deliver Lysa Arryn.

380
00:27:56,010 --> 00:27:58,380
I didn't need Janos Slynt.

381
00:28:01,170 --> 00:28:02,700
It's settled, then?

382
00:28:05,170 --> 00:28:06,290
Good.

383
00:28:08,520 --> 00:28:10,530
Oh, and remember...

384
00:28:10,530 --> 00:28:12,460
the queen mustn't know.

385
00:28:51,710 --> 00:28:53,450
That must hurt.

386
00:29:03,650 --> 00:29:04,700
What?

387
00:29:07,140 --> 00:29:08,330
What is it?

388
00:29:10,270 --> 00:29:12,460
A member of the kingsguard?

389
00:29:14,240 --> 00:29:16,340
As if I wasn't humiliated enough already.

390
00:29:18,680 --> 00:29:22,680
Brienne is a very capable warrior.

391
00:29:24,030 --> 00:29:25,530
And she's devoted to me.

392
00:29:28,110 --> 00:29:29,460
You're jealous.

393
00:29:31,430 --> 00:29:32,600
Jealous?

394
00:29:32,600 --> 00:29:34,580
Of Brienne the beauty?

395
00:29:35,330 --> 00:29:36,770
Don't make me laugh.

396
00:29:38,620 --> 00:29:40,240
I'll make it up to you.

397
00:29:40,960 --> 00:29:42,210
No, your grace.

398
00:29:43,240 --> 00:29:44,750
Not tonight.

399
00:29:45,780 --> 00:29:48,350
There's another Tyrell who requires your attention.

400
00:29:48,650 --> 00:29:52,600
You didn't win my father's support or his army on charm alone.

401
00:30:05,810 --> 00:30:08,700
Your vassals are starting to snigger behind your back.

402
00:30:09,830 --> 00:30:12,940
Brides aren't usually virgins two weeks after their wedding night.

403
00:30:13,030 --> 00:30:14,690
And Margaery's a virgin?

404
00:30:15,140 --> 00:30:16,060
Officially.

405
00:30:18,030 --> 00:30:19,560
Shall I bring her to you?

406
00:30:47,110 --> 00:30:50,500
I should warn you, I've had quite a bit of wine.

407
00:30:50,500 --> 00:30:52,560
As is your right. You are a king.

408
00:30:55,460 --> 00:30:56,770
You look very beautiful.

409
00:30:58,020 --> 00:30:59,150
Thank you, your grace.

410
00:31:00,130 --> 00:31:01,390
It's a lovely gown.

411
00:31:01,540 --> 00:31:02,800
You think so?

412
00:31:03,960 --> 00:31:06,050
I can't decide how I like it better.

413
00:31:06,050 --> 00:31:06,920
This way...

414
00:31:08,040 --> 00:31:11,030
Or this way.

415
00:31:17,240 --> 00:31:18,880
You certainly don't need it.

416
00:31:20,580 --> 00:31:21,260
Although...

417
00:31:21,990 --> 00:31:27,650
Some say that beauty most desired is the beauty concealed.

418
00:31:44,160 --> 00:31:45,280
Must be the wine.

419
00:31:46,340 --> 00:31:48,210
Here, let me.

420
00:32:08,720 --> 00:32:09,840
I'm sorry.

421
00:32:11,330 --> 00:32:13,460
Do you want my brother to come in and help?

422
00:32:16,510 --> 00:32:17,340
What?

423
00:32:17,340 --> 00:32:18,500
He could get you started.

424
00:32:18,500 --> 00:32:19,900
I know he wouldn't mind.

425
00:32:19,900 --> 00:32:22,320
Or I can turn over and you can pretend I'm him.

426
00:32:24,790 --> 00:32:26,880
I don't know what you're talking about.

427
00:32:32,520 --> 00:32:34,950
There's no need for us to play games.

428
00:32:35,710 --> 00:32:38,730
Save your lies for court. You're going to need a lot of them.

429
00:32:57,100 --> 00:32:59,570
Your enemies aren't happy about us.

430
00:33:00,390 --> 00:33:02,060
They want to tear us apart.

431
00:33:02,210 --> 00:33:04,430
And the best way to stop them

432
00:33:05,550 --> 00:33:07,270
is to put your baby

433
00:33:08,720 --> 00:33:10,170
in my belly.

434
00:33:14,030 --> 00:33:15,790
We can try again later.

435
00:33:16,740 --> 00:33:18,510
You decide how you want to do it...

436
00:33:18,510 --> 00:33:20,230
With me, with me and Loras.

437
00:33:20,230 --> 00:33:21,780
However else you like.

438
00:33:25,500 --> 00:33:27,310
Whatever you need to do.

439
00:33:29,890 --> 00:33:32,430
You are a king.

440
00:33:41,740 --> 00:33:42,920
You monster.

441
00:33:44,310 --> 00:33:46,180
Myrcella is my only daughter.

442
00:33:46,180 --> 00:33:48,960
Do you really think I'll let you sell her like a common whore?

443
00:33:48,960 --> 00:33:50,540
Myrcella's a princess.

444
00:33:50,540 --> 00:33:52,050
Some would say she was born for this.

445
00:33:52,050 --> 00:33:53,820
I will not let you ship her off to Dorne

446
00:33:53,820 --> 00:33:55,990
as I was shipped off to Robert Baratheon.

447
00:33:55,990 --> 00:33:58,340
Dorne is the safest place for her.

448
00:33:58,630 --> 00:34:01,630
Are you mad? The Martells loathe us.

449
00:34:01,800 --> 00:34:03,940
That's why we need to seduce them.

450
00:34:03,940 --> 00:34:05,890
We're going to need their support in the war

451
00:34:05,890 --> 00:34:07,700
your son started.

452
00:34:07,700 --> 00:34:10,380
- She'll be a hostage. - A guest.

453
00:34:11,040 --> 00:34:12,590
You won't get away with this.

454
00:34:13,380 --> 00:34:16,610
You think the piece of paper father gave you keeps you safe.

455
00:34:19,600 --> 00:34:21,860
Ned Stark had a piece of paper, too.

456
00:34:24,350 --> 00:34:25,860
- It's done, Cersei. - No.

457
00:34:27,260 --> 00:34:28,800
You cannot stop it.

458
00:34:28,800 --> 00:34:29,940
No!

459
00:34:33,450 --> 00:34:36,460
Just how safe do you think Myrcella is if this city falls?

460
00:34:36,460 --> 00:34:38,180
Do you want to see her raped,

461
00:34:38,180 --> 00:34:40,170
butchered like the Targaryen children?

462
00:34:40,650 --> 00:34:42,010
Make no mistake.

463
00:34:42,440 --> 00:34:45,220
They'll mount her pretty little head on a spike right beside yours.

464
00:34:45,220 --> 00:34:47,440
Get out! Get out!

465
00:35:49,740 --> 00:35:51,640
Theon of the House Greyjoy,

466
00:35:52,370 --> 00:35:56,000
you would this day consecrate your faith to the Drowned God?

467
00:36:03,880 --> 00:36:05,010
I would.

468
00:36:05,410 --> 00:36:06,440
Kneel.

469
00:36:09,880 --> 00:36:11,210
Let Theon, your servant,

470
00:36:11,210 --> 00:36:13,830
be born again from the sea as you were.

471
00:36:14,880 --> 00:36:16,610
Bless him with salt.

472
00:36:19,480 --> 00:36:21,190
Bless him with stone.

473
00:36:22,540 --> 00:36:24,340
Bless him with steel.

474
00:36:29,560 --> 00:36:31,410
What is dead may never die.

475
00:36:31,410 --> 00:36:33,310
What is dead may never die...

476
00:36:35,140 --> 00:36:38,560
But rises again harder and stronger.

477
00:36:39,540 --> 00:36:40,660
Stand.

478
00:37:09,770 --> 00:37:12,870
I don't appreciate being made a fool of, dwarf.

479
00:37:14,100 --> 00:37:15,610
If Myrcella marries the Martell boy,

480
00:37:15,610 --> 00:37:18,220
she can't very well marry Robin Arryn, can she?

481
00:37:18,220 --> 00:37:21,200
No, afraid not. Sorry about that.

482
00:37:21,200 --> 00:37:22,290
And Harrenhal...

483
00:37:23,110 --> 00:37:26,170
I suppose that's off the table as well.

484
00:37:26,170 --> 00:37:29,890
Yes, I fear so. Sorry about that, too.

485
00:37:29,890 --> 00:37:31,980
Leave me out of your next deception.

486
00:37:31,980 --> 00:37:34,140
Oh, that's a shame.

487
00:37:34,390 --> 00:37:36,970
You were to be the centerpiece of my next deception.

488
00:37:37,620 --> 00:37:40,500
My brother Jaime rots in a northern stockade.

489
00:37:41,100 --> 00:37:42,840
I would see him released.

490
00:37:43,380 --> 00:37:44,480
that's where you come in.

491
00:37:44,480 --> 00:37:47,050
Robb Stark will never release the Kingslayer.

492
00:37:47,050 --> 00:37:50,360
No, he won't. But his mother might.

493
00:37:51,420 --> 00:37:54,240
How would you like to see your beloved Cat again?

494
00:37:57,360 --> 00:37:59,570
- Find him? - Oh, Aye.

495
00:37:59,570 --> 00:38:01,200
And he has company.

496
00:38:02,980 --> 00:38:05,880
Filthy old stoat. Almost hate to interrupt.

497
00:38:05,880 --> 00:38:07,060
No, you don't.

498
00:38:07,680 --> 00:38:08,980
No, I don't.

499
00:38:16,390 --> 00:38:18,050
What is the meaning of this?

500
00:38:18,730 --> 00:38:20,570
No, please, please.

501
00:38:21,090 --> 00:38:23,070
You disappoint me, Grand Maester.

502
00:38:23,070 --> 00:38:25,150
I am your loyal servant.

503
00:38:25,370 --> 00:38:27,860
So loyal that you told the Queen about my plans to

504
00:38:27,860 --> 00:38:29,360
send Myrcella to Dorne.

505
00:38:29,360 --> 00:38:31,090
No! Never!

506
00:38:31,560 --> 00:38:33,840
It's a falsehood. I swear it.

507
00:38:33,840 --> 00:38:35,250
It wasn't me.

508
00:38:35,970 --> 00:38:37,540
Ah, Varys.

509
00:38:37,540 --> 00:38:40,380
It was Varys the spider.

510
00:38:40,380 --> 00:38:44,880
See, I told varys that I was giving the princess to the Greyjoys.

511
00:38:44,880 --> 00:38:49,100
I told littlefinger that I planned to wed her to Robin Arryn.

512
00:38:49,270 --> 00:38:52,660
I told no one that I was offering her to the Dornish.

513
00:38:53,320 --> 00:38:54,400
No one but you.

514
00:38:54,400 --> 00:38:57,640
The eunuch has spies everywhere.

515
00:38:57,640 --> 00:38:59,790
Cut off his manhood and feed it to the goats.

516
00:38:59,790 --> 00:39:02,490
- No, no, no. - There are no goats, halfman.

517
00:39:02,490 --> 00:39:04,080
Well, make do.

518
00:39:06,620 --> 00:39:09,250
How long have you been spying for my sister?

519
00:39:09,250 --> 00:39:11,980
All I did, I did for House Lannister.

520
00:39:11,980 --> 00:39:14,220
Always. Your lord father, ask him.

521
00:39:14,220 --> 00:39:15,980
I've always been his servant

522
00:39:15,980 --> 00:39:18,290
since the days of the Mad King.

523
00:39:19,900 --> 00:39:21,250
I don't like his beard.

524
00:39:21,250 --> 00:39:22,060
What?

525
00:39:22,350 --> 00:39:25,070
What? Oh, no. No.

526
00:39:28,500 --> 00:39:30,930
How many Hands have you betrayed, Pycelle?

527
00:39:30,930 --> 00:39:32,610
Eddard Stark? Jon Arryn?

528
00:39:32,610 --> 00:39:35,300
Lord Arryn, he knew.

529
00:39:35,300 --> 00:39:38,130
He knew the truth about the queen.

530
00:39:38,130 --> 00:39:41,600
And, well, he planned to act,

531
00:39:41,600 --> 00:39:43,650
to tell King Robert.

532
00:39:43,650 --> 00:39:45,090
So you poisoned him?

533
00:39:45,480 --> 00:39:47,240
No. Never.

534
00:39:47,240 --> 00:39:49,900
But you let him die, made sure he succumbed.

535
00:39:49,900 --> 00:39:52,990
Lannister... I always served Lannister.

536
00:39:52,990 --> 00:39:55,430
Get him out of my sight. Throw him in one of the black cells.

537
00:39:55,430 --> 00:39:57,220
Oh, no. No, no, no. No, please.

538
00:39:57,220 --> 00:39:59,290
Don't! You can't do this to me!

539
00:40:00,760 --> 00:40:02,290
For your trouble.

540
00:40:26,900 --> 00:40:29,170
You'll be pleased to know our mutual friend

541
00:40:29,170 --> 00:40:32,510
is doing quite well in lady Sansa's service.

542
00:40:33,070 --> 00:40:35,940
Good. One of my better ideas.

543
00:40:35,940 --> 00:40:40,680
And it seems the Grand Maester has found his way into a black cell.

544
00:40:42,850 --> 00:40:45,090
Well played, my lord Hand.

545
00:40:46,360 --> 00:40:48,690
But should I be worried?

546
00:40:48,690 --> 00:40:51,100
Janos Slynt, Pycelle...

547
00:40:51,100 --> 00:40:53,740
The small council grows smaller every day.

548
00:40:53,740 --> 00:40:57,140
The council has a reputation for serving past Hands poorly.

549
00:40:57,140 --> 00:41:00,220
I don't mean to follow Ned Stark to the grave.

550
00:41:00,990 --> 00:41:04,110
Power is a curious thing, my lord.

551
00:41:05,160 --> 00:41:06,670
Are you fond of riddles?

552
00:41:06,670 --> 00:41:08,760
Why, am I about to hear one?

553
00:41:08,760 --> 00:41:11,040
Three great men sit in a room.

554
00:41:11,040 --> 00:41:14,040
A king, a priest and a rich man.

555
00:41:14,040 --> 00:41:17,010
Between them stands a common sellsword.

556
00:41:17,010 --> 00:41:21,050
Each great man bids the sellsword kill the other two.

557
00:41:21,050 --> 00:41:23,310
Who lives, who dies?

558
00:41:24,260 --> 00:41:25,840
Depends on the sellsword.

559
00:41:25,840 --> 00:41:28,840
Does it? He has neither crown nor gold

560
00:41:28,840 --> 00:41:30,250
nor favor with the gods.

561
00:41:30,250 --> 00:41:32,160
He has a sword, the power of life and death.

562
00:41:32,160 --> 00:41:34,380
But if it's swordsmen who rule,

563
00:41:34,380 --> 00:41:37,520
why do we pretend kings hold all the power?

564
00:41:37,520 --> 00:41:39,960
When Ned Stark lost his head,

565
00:41:39,960 --> 00:41:42,040
who was truly responsible?

566
00:41:42,570 --> 00:41:45,220
Joffrey? The executioner?

567
00:41:45,220 --> 00:41:46,630
Or something else?

568
00:41:46,630 --> 00:41:48,790
I've decided I don't like riddles.

569
00:41:51,780 --> 00:41:56,030
Power resides where men believe it resides.

570
00:41:57,040 --> 00:41:58,300
It's a trick,

571
00:41:58,300 --> 00:42:00,120
a shadow on the wall.

572
00:42:01,070 --> 00:42:07,600
And a very small man can cast a very large shadow.

573
00:42:47,460 --> 00:42:49,030
You should be sleeping.

574
00:42:50,450 --> 00:42:52,180
Tomorrow's a long march.

575
00:42:53,650 --> 00:42:56,160
30 miles if it don't piss on us.

576
00:42:57,560 --> 00:42:59,070
I can't sleep.

577
00:43:03,770 --> 00:43:05,290
I don't like the taste.

578
00:43:08,530 --> 00:43:14,840
Well... you don't drink it for the flavor, to be honest.

579
00:43:22,840 --> 00:43:23,880
What?

580
00:43:25,410 --> 00:43:26,910
How do you sleep?

581
00:43:27,600 --> 00:43:29,540
Same as most men, I think.

582
00:43:30,290 --> 00:43:32,840
But you've seen things,

583
00:43:33,950 --> 00:43:35,380
horrible things.

584
00:43:36,600 --> 00:43:37,560
Aye.

585
00:43:39,180 --> 00:43:41,470
I've seen some pretty things, too,

586
00:43:42,080 --> 00:43:43,350
but not nearly so many.

587
00:43:45,470 --> 00:43:47,090
How do you sleep when you...

588
00:43:49,610 --> 00:43:53,820
when you have those things in your head?

589
00:43:55,980 --> 00:43:58,050
You didn't see that.

590
00:43:58,930 --> 00:44:00,350
I made damn sure.

591
00:44:00,350 --> 00:44:02,570
I close my eyes and I see them up there.

592
00:44:04,250 --> 00:44:05,290
All of them

593
00:44:06,410 --> 00:44:07,690
standing there...

594
00:44:09,350 --> 00:44:10,410
Joffrey,

595
00:44:12,740 --> 00:44:13,780
The Queen,

596
00:44:14,260 --> 00:44:15,080
and...

597
00:44:17,220 --> 00:44:18,530
and my sister.

598
00:44:27,810 --> 00:44:31,980
You know, we've got something in common, me and you.

599
00:44:31,980 --> 00:44:32,850
You know that?

600
00:44:34,370 --> 00:44:35,940
I must have been

601
00:44:37,160 --> 00:44:39,060
a couple of years older than you.

602
00:44:41,540 --> 00:44:45,210
I saw my brother stabbed through the heart right on our doorstep.

603
00:44:46,250 --> 00:44:48,590
He weren't much of a villain what skewered him.

604
00:44:49,700 --> 00:44:51,830
Willem, the lad's name was.

605
00:44:53,590 --> 00:44:56,120
He ran off before anyone could spit.

606
00:44:57,530 --> 00:44:59,110
And I just stood there,

607
00:45:00,450 --> 00:45:02,200
watching my brother die.

608
00:45:04,090 --> 00:45:06,210
But here's the funny part.

609
00:45:07,360 --> 00:45:10,410
I can't picture my brother's face anymore.

610
00:45:11,250 --> 00:45:12,220
But Willem...

611
00:45:13,150 --> 00:45:15,470
Oh, he was a nice-looking boy.

612
00:45:17,580 --> 00:45:19,320
He had good white teeth,

613
00:45:20,070 --> 00:45:21,370
blue eyes,

614
00:45:22,370 --> 00:45:25,640
One of those dimpled chins all the girls like.

615
00:45:28,140 --> 00:45:30,450
I would think about him when I was working,

616
00:45:31,410 --> 00:45:34,090
when I was drinking, when I was having a shit.

617
00:45:35,460 --> 00:45:37,020
It got to the point

618
00:45:37,610 --> 00:45:40,850
where I would say his name every night before I went to bed.

619
00:45:40,850 --> 00:45:44,760
Willem. Willem. Willem.

620
00:45:46,120 --> 00:45:47,730
A prayer almost.

621
00:45:50,180 --> 00:45:51,190
Well, one day...

622
00:45:53,860 --> 00:45:56,560
Willem came riding back into town.

623
00:46:00,680 --> 00:46:03,620
I buried an ax so deep into Willem's skull,

624
00:46:03,620 --> 00:46:06,680
they had to bury him with it.

625
00:46:09,540 --> 00:46:11,300
Willem's horse got me to the Wall

626
00:46:11,300 --> 00:46:14,000
and I've been wearing black ever since.

627
00:46:18,190 --> 00:46:19,280
Well...

628
00:46:19,960 --> 00:46:21,900
that'll help you sleep, eh?

629
00:46:30,640 --> 00:46:33,750
Get up, you lazy sons of whores!

630
00:46:33,750 --> 00:46:35,580
Arm yourselves.

631
00:46:36,940 --> 00:46:38,120
- Get up. - Get up.

632
00:46:39,170 --> 00:46:40,540
Keep out of sight, both of you.

633
00:46:40,540 --> 00:46:41,660
- No, I'm not afraid. - I can fight.

634
00:46:41,660 --> 00:46:43,750
Keep out of sight.

635
00:46:44,320 --> 00:46:46,590
If things go wrong, you run.

636
00:46:46,590 --> 00:46:51,050
Do you hear me? You run along north and don't look back.

637
00:46:51,050 --> 00:46:55,510
Hey, there's men out there who want to fuck your corpses.

638
00:46:55,800 --> 00:46:58,140
Outside, now!

639
00:47:00,450 --> 00:47:02,060
Come on, move, move!

640
00:47:04,270 --> 00:47:05,360
Gold cloaks!

641
00:47:10,670 --> 00:47:12,020
Everyone out!

642
00:47:17,130 --> 00:47:20,510
Hey, you! Open the damn cage!

643
00:47:23,840 --> 00:47:25,560
Where's the bastard, crow?

644
00:47:25,560 --> 00:47:28,050
Got more than a few bastards here. Who's asking?

645
00:47:28,050 --> 00:47:31,510
Ser Amory Lorch, sworn bannerman to lord Tywin Lannister.

646
00:47:31,750 --> 00:47:34,950
These men from the capital requested our assistance.

647
00:47:35,370 --> 00:47:37,420
Drop your weapons in the name of the king.

648
00:47:37,810 --> 00:47:39,460
Now, which king would that be?

649
00:47:39,460 --> 00:47:41,280
This is your last chance.

650
00:47:42,050 --> 00:47:44,270
In the name of King Joffrey,

651
00:47:44,660 --> 00:47:46,360
drop your weapons.

652
00:47:49,970 --> 00:47:51,410
I don't think I will.

653
00:47:52,050 --> 00:47:53,320
So be it.

654
00:47:56,810 --> 00:47:58,950
I always hated crossbows.

655
00:47:58,950 --> 00:48:00,920
Take too long to load.

656
00:48:38,580 --> 00:48:40,250
Boy, come here. Boy!

657
00:48:40,420 --> 00:48:43,630
- Sweet boy, help us. - Come back here!

658
00:48:44,190 --> 00:48:45,380
Help us, boy!

659
00:48:49,250 --> 00:48:52,240
A man can fight! Free us!

660
00:48:58,920 --> 00:49:00,880
Quick, give it to me.

661
00:49:02,120 --> 00:49:03,650
Give me the ax. Give me that.

662
00:49:13,340 --> 00:49:14,740
Put 'em on the wagon!

663
00:49:16,070 --> 00:49:17,240
There's more here. Come on.

664
00:49:22,940 --> 00:49:24,510
What do we have here?

665
00:49:26,300 --> 00:49:27,200
No!

666
00:49:28,470 --> 00:49:30,120
That's a fine little blade.

667
00:49:32,340 --> 00:49:34,050
Maybe I'll pick my teeth with it.

668
00:49:34,050 --> 00:49:35,720
I yield! I yield!

669
00:49:35,720 --> 00:49:37,690
Round up any survivors.

670
00:49:38,080 --> 00:49:40,210
We'll take them back to Harrenhal.

671
00:49:40,210 --> 00:49:42,720
You heard him. You're coming with us.

672
00:49:43,900 --> 00:49:44,910
I yield!

673
00:49:50,860 --> 00:49:51,830
Help!

674
00:49:51,830 --> 00:49:53,210
Help me!

675
00:49:57,740 --> 00:49:59,540
Something wrong with your leg, boy?

676
00:49:59,540 --> 00:50:00,870
Look at it.

677
00:50:09,430 --> 00:50:10,470
Can you walk?

678
00:50:11,260 --> 00:50:13,330
No. You got to carry me.

679
00:50:14,860 --> 00:50:15,690
All right.

680
00:50:30,470 --> 00:50:31,880
Carry him, he says.

681
00:50:41,380 --> 00:50:43,710
We're looking for a bastard named Gendry.

682
00:50:44,710 --> 00:50:45,740
Give him up

683
00:50:46,640 --> 00:50:49,080
or I'll start taking eyeballs.

684
00:51:01,950 --> 00:51:03,370
You want Gendry?

685
00:51:07,130 --> 00:51:08,530
You already got him.

686
00:51:13,080 --> 00:51:14,960
He loved that helmet.

